# GitHub Pages reads public/CNAME literally to decide the custom domain, and
# this repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf on. Git already stores
# the blob as LF, but without this a checkout would put CRLF in the working
# copy, and a local `npm run build` would then produce a dist/CNAME whose
# hostname ends in a stray carriage return.
CNAME text eol=lf
